<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to May 16.</p>
<p>Top 10 gains in year    Price     percent</p>
<p>Rank Name		   May 16    change</p>
<p>1   Oil Search	     2.80	118.75</p>
<p>2   Sthn Pac Pete	  3.55	108.82</p>
<p>3   Howard Smith	  11.90	 70.00</p>
<p>4   James Hardie	   4.05	 61.35</p>
<p>5   CSL Limited	    7.40	 61.22</p>
<p>6   Fletcher Energy	4.20	 60.31</p>
<p>7   Natl Aust Bank	17.95	 55.28</p>
<p>8   Woodside Pet	  11.20	 53.85</p>
<p>9   Aust Gas Light	 7.40	 52.26</p>
<p>10  Transurban	   950.00	 52.24</p>
<p>Top 10 falls in year    Price     percent</p>
<p>Rank Name		   May 16    change</p>
<p>1   Newcrest		 3.40	-40.46</p>
<p>2   Acacia		   1.95	-38.68</p>
<p>3   Sons of Gwalia	 5.75	-36.81</p>
<p>4   Goldfields	     2.07	-33.44</p>
<p>5   Great Cen Mines	2.60	-33.33</p>
<p>6   Plutonic		 5.04	-29.01</p>
<p>7   Davids		   1.27	-28.25</p>
<p>8   Normandy		 1.60	-27.93</p>
<p>9   QNI			2.54	-19.87</p>
<p>10  Caltex		   4.30	-18.87</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
